This source package is exported from the local ffmpeg-rockchip-81 repository's
rockchip-8.0 branch with git archive, then this debian/ directory is overlaid by
the YSP packaging script. The source is based on the official n8.0.3 tag and
adds the RKMPP/RKRGA forward-port and hardening series.

The Debian version starts with `7:8.0.3`. The epoch matches Ubuntu's FFmpeg
packaging, while the upstream portion accurately identifies the source release.
The Rockchip git snapshot follows as a `+rockchip+git...` suffix.

The package keeps the normal Ubuntu/Debian FFmpeg feature surface and library
package names: libavcodec62, libavdevice62, libavfilter11, libavformat62,
libavutil60, libswresample6, and libswscale9. The standard symbols templates
remain active, while RKMPP, RKRGA, libdrm, and version3 support are enabled for
the Rockchip arm64 build.
